            "text": "{\"study_topic_id\":\"study-47d32cbcc129ff9aa679\",\"overview\":{\"text\":\"Artificial intelligence (AI) is a research field within computer science concerned with building systems that perform tasks associated with intelligence, such as learning from experience, solving problems, recognizing patterns, planning, or working with language. It is not one particular kind of machine: AI includes approaches ranging from programs that use explicit logic and rules to machine-learning systems that improve through data. Machine learning is therefore a branch of AI, not a synonym for the whole field. The term was coined by computer scientist John McCarthy in 1955; a 1956 Dartmouth workshop helped establish the emerging field, though participants disagreed about how to create intelligent machines. AI can imitate selected abilities without necessarily thinking as people do.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/brief-definitions-of-key-terms-in-ai\",\"https://computerhistory.org/stories/chatbots-decoded/\"]},\"key_facts\":[{\"text\":\"Computer scientist John McCarthy coined the term “AI” in 1955.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://computerhistory.org/profile/john-mccarthy/\"]},{\"text\":\"At a 1956 Dartmouth workshop, researchers named the emerging field artificial intelligence, but disagreed about how to build intelligent machines.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://computerhistory.org/stories/chatbots-decoded/\"]},{\"text\":\"Machine learning is one part of AI: it studies how systems can improve their perception, decisions, or actions using experience or data.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/brief-definitions-of-key-terms-in-ai\"]},{\"text\":\"Symbolic AI uses logic and rules to work with symbols; neural networks are a different approach, loosely inspired by brain structures.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://computerhistory.org/stories/chatbots-decoded/\"]},{\"text\":\"Narrow AI focuses on particular tasks, while artificial general intelligence describes the aim of broadly capable, context-aware machines.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/brief-definitions-of-key-terms-in-ai\"]}],\"sources\":[{\"title\":\"Brief Definitions of Key Terms in AI\",\"url\":\"https://hai.stanford.edu/policy/brief-definitions-of-key-terms-in-ai\",\"publisher\":\"Stanford Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence (Stanford HAI)\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:48:29.768740+00:00\",\"supports\":\"Definitions of AI and machine learning; learning methods; distinction between narrow AI and artificial general intelligence.\"},{\"title\":\"Chatbots Decoded\",\"url\":\"https://computerhistory.org/stories/chatbots-decoded/\",\"publisher\":\"Computer History Museum\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:48:29.768740+00:00\",\"supports\":\"AI’s early history, the 1956 Dartmouth workshop, symbolic AI, neural networks, and their brain-inspired design.\"},{\"title\":\"John McCarthy\",\"url\":\"https://computerhistory.org/profile/john-mccarthy/\",\"publisher\":\"Computer History Museum\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:48:29.768740+00:00\",\"supports\":\"John McCarthy’s role in cofounding AI and coining the term in 1955.\"}],\"research_queries\":[\"site:computerhistory.org artificial intelligence definition history AI learning reasoning\",\"site:ai.gov artificial intelligence definition machine learning official\",\"site:hai.stanford.edu what is artificial intelligence machine learning definition\"],\"notes\":\"The overview is 117 words. Claims are supported by directly opened Stanford HAI and Computer History Museum pages; each key fact includes its supporting page URL.\",\"unresolved_concerns\":[],\"self_check_complete\":true}"
          }
